# Code owners for the files that decide what NetRelish is allowed to ship.
#
# This file blocks nothing on its own. It only takes effect as a gate once "Require review
# from Code Owners" is turned on for main in the repository's branch protection (or ruleset).
# Until then, GitHub uses it only to request the owner's review on pull requests that touch
# these paths.
#
# The repository belongs to the Shepdesign-LLC organization. An organization cannot be a code
# owner (only people and teams can), so the maintainer's account is listed. If a team is
# created later, list the team here instead.
#
# One thing to know before turning the requirement on: nobody can approve their own pull
# request. With a single maintainer, pull requests opened from the maintainer's own account
# would need a second reviewer or a bypass rule.

# Workflows, the CodeQL query pack, and this file
/.github/                                             @Shepdesign

# The endpoint gate (non-negotiable 5) and the tests that prove it
/scripts/codeql_gate.py                               @Shepdesign
/scripts/tests/                                       @Shepdesign

# Build settings and what the signed app is entitled to do
/Config/                                              @Shepdesign
/NetRelish.entitlements                               @Shepdesign
/Sources/ShareExtension/NetRelishShare.entitlements   @Shepdesign

# Third-party code that runs inside pages being captured, and its recorded checksum
/Resources/Extraction/                                @Shepdesign
/scripts/checksums/                                   @Shepdesign
